    <!-- Tutorial hints (keys come from game/Tutorial.kt) -->
    <string name="tut_tap_spell">Tap a spell below to cast it. Its row number (1–5) is the lane it flies along.</string>
    <string name="tut_watch_shot">Casting takes a moment. Then your spell flies down its lane and pushes that row to the far side.</string>
    <string name="tut_make_line">Line up 3 or more of the same element in a row or a column. They explode and hit your opponent.</string>
    <string name="tut_damage">Each exploded globe deals 5 damage. Falling globes can set off chain explosions: ×2, ×3…</string>
    <string name="tut_backfire">That row was full, so your spell backfired and hit you. Aim at rows with space.</string>
    <string name="tut_walls_tap">New: walls! Tap a wall button above the field. After a long cast, magic glass fills every empty cell of that column.</string>
    <string name="tut_walls_break">A shot that reaches a wall breaks it and stops there. Globes pushed against a wall stop too, but if the row in front of it is full, the push breaks the wall. An explosion breaks the walls next to it.</string>
